infographic sequence-ascending-steps
data
  title Timeout ladder: retire before something else kills it
  desc Ordered shortest to longest — each pool control must fire before the external timeout it guards against
  order asc
  sequences
    - label Keepalive probe — under 350 s
      desc Pool pings idle connections before the NAT can drop them; the interval must beat the middlebox idle limit.
    - label NAT / firewall idle — about 350 s
      desc External: a stateful firewall silently drops the idle flow, and afterwards packets vanish into a black hole.
    - label idleTimeout — 10 min
      desc Pool evicts spare idle connections off-peak — only acts when minimumIdle is set below the maximum.
    - label maxLifetime — 30 min
      desc Pool retires every connection by age, proactively, whether or not it still looks healthy.
    - label MySQL wait_timeout — 8 h
      desc External: the server closes its backend unannounced, so maxLifetime must fire first and the pool closes before this does.
theme
  palette #14b8a6 #f59e0b #f43f5e
